👑🧠 Birbal and the Cold Water Challenge (Raw Story)

One winter day, Emperor Akbar challenged his court.

He said, “If anyone can stand in the cold river all night, I will reward them.”

A poor man agreed.

He stood in the freezing water all night.

The next morning, he came to Akbar for his reward.

Akbar asked, “How did you manage to stay in the cold?”

The man said, “I kept looking at a distant light.”

Akbar said, “Then you got warmth from that light. You will not get the reward.”

The man felt very sad.

Birbal heard about this.

The next day, Birbal set up a pot far above a small fire.

Akbar asked, “How will the food cook like that?”

Birbal said, “If a distant light can give warmth, then this fire can cook the food too.”

Akbar understood his mistake.

He rewarded the poor man.

💖 Moral:

Always be fair and think wisely before judging others.
